  "music": "w4-castle-clatter",
  "authorNotes": "Two players required — this is the world's team gate. lever-w4-07-outer (latching) raises door-w4-07-outer, a warmup gate either player can solo, then swing-approach carries both individually to pier 2 (870-1470), same shape as 02/03. The genuine gate is the next gap: pier 2 to pier 3 is 410px, past what any single swing in this world covers. The solve is the same 'throw a friend' from W1-07: both players pump swing-anchor (pivot 1550,650, 200px reach) together, and at the top of the arc one lets go, throwing the other the rest of the way to pier 3's edge; the thrower follows on the assist beam or their own swing of swing-anchor a second time. This is why the level cannot start with one player — nothing here is solvable alone. Below pier 3, rope-w4-07-drop hangs down to a small two-ledge alcove (a bonus room, not on the critical path): lever-w4-07-x and lever-w4-07-y sit 310px apart, further than one body's two arms can hold at once (full reach is 118px per arm), so relay-w4-07-and (op and) only fires 'w4-07-relic-gate' when two players hold their respective levers at the same instant. door-w4-07-relic (a small sliding panel, openOffset on x rather than y since this one is a horizontal grille) then opens; relic-w4-07 sits just 60px from lever-w4-07-y, within the same player's free arm's reach, so whoever is anchoring lever-y can snag it one-handed the moment the door opens without letting go — no one needs to release early and no one needs a third body. Back up top, swing-final-07 (260px) finishes the crossing to the goal pier, both players and the relic together. Checkpoints sit after pier 2 and after pier 3 so a failed throw or a failed relic grab doesn't cost the whole run."
